{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter","id":607106,"title":"Concept: Werewolf hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-29T14:33:54-07:00","id":607106,"title":"Concept: Werewolf hunter","content":"So, in about a year or so there's a new game for 2nd Ed. coming out, it's a crossover style game, and I was thinking of making a Gangrel, kind of a keeper of the peace between werewolves and vampires, and if needed, a protector of the vampires.<br /> <br /> Now, to do this, I need to be able to actually stand up to a werewolf. I know they are ridiculous machines of war. It's not likely a vampire can stand toe to toe with them, especially one built for combat, but I am trying to do my best.<br /> <br /> Thus far, stat wise, I was going so start with Str 4 Dex 3 Stam 3, Brawl 4: Specialty Feral Combat, standard faire. Disciplines, I was thinking Protean 3 right off the bat, and first buy is protean 4 + Claws of the unholy. Merit wise, starting off with Riding the Wave fighting style 2 or 3 depending on restricted slots, and blood potency 3. For covenant, I was going Ordo Dracul. Coil of the Wyrm. I've always been fascinated by the beast, and I think that it would be a good roleplaying choice as well for a Gangrel focused on dealing with other beasts.<br /> <br /> So, let's break down the stats.<br /> <br /> Str 4, Brawl 4, Specialty. That's 9 dice, base. BP 3 = 3 blood, +wp = 3 dice, that's 18 dice. In frenzy, you gain your BP to your strength, so that's 21 dice. Weapon is +0, so that's no bonus, but the damage would be aggravated to bypass the werewolf automatic regeneration. The character has little defense, maybe take brawling dodge and we would have like, a 7 defense at most.<br /> <br /> So, do you think this could take out a standard combat focused werewolf?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","name":"Regentwill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:56:57-07:00","id":607161,"title":"","content":"You'd only have your Dex or Wits for Defense, but sure, that's enough to kill a werewolf or dust a vampire or do whatever happens to strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:00:35-07:00","id":607166,"title":"","content":"I just re-read the frenzy rules, where does it say you lose Athletics / brawl to defense? I must have missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","name":"Regentwill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:01:58-07:00","id":607168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Regentwill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter#post607106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think this could take out a standard combat focused werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off hand, a purity 4 Rahu would be able to grapple and bind you, and then use Efficient Killer to take you out right away. Auto successes are powerful, and Full Moon/Rage/Strength Gifts are easily a match for any bonuses from Protean claws. Toss in some Glory and merits for some damage reduction and armor? It doesn't look good for the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Using hit and run tactics with Protean, swapping to bat form, or melding with the ground, is better than a straight up fight with Protean against a wolf.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if you want a pure slug fest, you're better off using a silver axe and Vigor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-29-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:03:39-07:00","id":607170,"title":"","content":"So, MCN, what would you suggest? Should I try to throw in some vigor?<br /> <br /> Having Silver weapons would be awesome for a slug fest, but would be terror for relations, don't you think? The character isn't designed to be a killer, outright. But a protector, a mediator that is able to throw down if push comes to shove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","user":"Regentwill","date":". 07-29-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","name":"Regentwill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:21:26-07:00","id":607175,"title":"","content":"First off, peruse <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage\">this thread</a>, it's a Forsaken thread but does a lot of talking about feral, wolf vs vampire combat.<br /> <br /> Second, are you committed to the idea of fighting Werewolves in direct, claw-to-claw combat? Because in the long run that's their territory and Werewolves absolutely excel at it.<br /> <br /> The above build seems less like a vampire meant to hunt Werewolves and more like one who can butt heads with them and talk in their terms. Which, given what you are aiming for, might work better. If the aim is to be able to bruise and bite with the pack, proving vampires aren't some gamma predators to be pushed around, then this is probably the way to go. However, as I said, if the aim is to kill Uratha who cross you, there are better ways to go about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: read your last post. Yeah, that looks appropriate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-29-2015, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:37:16-07:00","id":607193,"title":"","content":"IMHO all depends on the &quot;Experience&quot; you give in the built of the two character (vampire and werewolf facing each other). To try to analyze the full power charachter of any race in order to make a totally ipotetical confrontation, and if you want to put the challange just on physical skills I tried to make a simulation about the respective pool:<br /> <br /> For the vampire we consider 5 strgt 5 Brawl 5 BP and 5-4 Athletics, 5 at celerity Vigor and resilence with protean for the Claw and the Unholy Claw.<br /> Same for the werewolf attribute and skills and for the gift i consider: CRIMSON SPASM (add the success on a 15 pool rolls to his strgt so we consider a mean of 8 more dot in strt), BERSERKER\u2019S MIGHT (reduce the damage inflicted by a single source by his Glory Renown (so suppose 5)), Efficient Killer Merit (that private him of defense).<br /> <br /> Now the Vampire have the pool for the attack of (using ride the wave): 20+4 (using 2 vitae)= 24<br /> Werewolf in Gauru attack pool is: 8 str+8 for Crimson+5 brwl = 21<br /> The vampire defense could be. 4+5+5 (celerity)= 14<br /> Werewolf defense (that can't be used if he use Efficient Killer)= 4 wits + 5 athle= 9<br /> <br /> Now consider the werewolf attack first: he use Efficient killer, vampire active celerity and interrupt his attack with his own, so the werewolf can't apply his defense: 24 dice of aggravated damage PLUS 1 vitae to activate vigor and add 5 more dice for a total of 29 dice of aggravated damage......the werewolf can subtract 5 from the success in this dice roll.<br /> <br /> Now consider the case werewolf attack you (maybe cause you won't use the active power of celerity): he make 21+2 for the claw - 14 (vampire defense)= 9 lethal damage.....- 5 using resilence = 4 lethal damage...not so much....Edit: or maybe bashing I'm not sure<br /> <br /> All this to say that both the race have the chance for a fair &quot;duel&quot;.<br /> In the real case where you have to build a normal vampire you could chose different way to defeat a werewolf. Maybe using obfuscate and domination or majesty properly. Anyway all depends on the stats of your opponents.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyway without aggravated damage the story is so far different cause if you don't make more lethal damage of the health of the Gauru in one turn, in the enxt he will completely heal himself for free and you have to start again. In this way at long time you will finish vitae and die :P Or you could use obfuscate to go away or make some kind of backstabb, or dominate to let him go away and save your life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-29-2015, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:55:01-07:00","id":607199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Regentwill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607166#post607166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just re-read the frenzy rules, where does it say you lose Athletics / brawl to defense? I must have missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, that's a function of Gauru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Regentwill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607170#post607170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, MCN, what would you suggest? Should I try to throw in some vigor?</div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on what you're trying to do. Just using Protean for the claws is ignoring the first three levels. Protean is awesome at being a general survivor. You can meld into the ground or fly above as a bat, and launch ambushes from that position. Wall climbing, faster speed, flying. Use the whole of the Discipline in your fight, not just one dot.<br /> <br /> Hell, if we ignore the Claws of the Unholy merit, the actual power of the Protean 4 is when using the Damage manuever in grapples! Otherwise, its just a +0A weapon, offset by both the Gauru's full defense AND reduced by any natural armor they could pick up.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the vast majority of &quot;combat wolves&quot; (ie Rahu) are going to have +Purity dots to their health, have +Purity in automatic successes in any action, +Purity to their Strength (on top of form bonuses), 8-again to all attacks. Rage (Glory) reduces damage, there are ways to get up to +4L claws and 3/3 armor with just merits alone. And that's a starting PC wolf. Your all-out attacking claws (21 dice) are reduced by (Defense+Brawl, lets say 2+4) 6, so 15 dice. And that's assuming the Werewolf hasn't slammed you with the Submissive Condition, effectively leeching your willpower or preventing you from attacking first.<br /> <br /> That's an average of 5 successes, reduced by 3/3 armor and 1 from Strength (Glory) Gift*, for 1 agg with your huge attack. The Rahu's got, at minimum, 10 health, and that's with Stamina 1. Meanwhile, your defense is down to 2 against his attack, claws that deal +6L automatically, and you can't heal that without using less vitae in your attack. And that's starting Purity 2, Glory 1. We've got a merit that ignores mundane armor. It gets more lopsided as Renown grows.<br /> <br /> And all that is assuming a Rahu. An Irraka stealth killer using Efficient Killer merit and surprise attacks? Entirely different ballgame. You're off guard, so no Defense. She hits you for her dice pool as all automatic successes. That's going to be at least 10L.<br /> <br /> <br /> With a Protean user, you're going to need to think outside of the box in these kinds of fights. Its going to be hard, since your focus (shapeshifting) is where Werewolves excel. If that's not what you want to do...<br /> <br /> <br /> * Yes, I know that Claws of the Unholy says that its only reduced by Resilience. However, all these armor reductions are from magical sources, making them the Werewolf equivalent of Resilience, since they all stack together. If not, then increase the damage dealt by 2 or 3, which, against a Rahu, is minimal when you're taking around 8 or 9L a turn and your opponent has over 10 health.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having Silver weapons would be awesome for a slug fest, but would be terror for relations, don't you think? The character isn't designed to be a killer, outright. But a protector, a mediator that is able to throw down if push comes to shove. </div> </div> </div> I'm not seeing much room for negotiations with this character here. Bringing silver is a sure sign of aggression, yes, but, on the other hand, I'm fairly sure that they don't have silver-detecting powers either, so a hidden blade should work just as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-29-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:58:08-07:00","id":607202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Regentwill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607166#post607166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just re-read the frenzy rules, where does it say you lose Athletics / brawl to defense? I must have missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not in Frenzy, it's in Gauru form, which is the one you're concerned with. 'In normal combat, opponents count only their Dexterity or Wits to their Defense; they may not add the appropriate Skill (normally Athletics).'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T15:58:26-07:00","id":607203,"title":"","content":"It's not what you want, but I once built a Werewolf had hunter in Masquerade, and the key points were:<br /> -High perception rolls.<br /> -Maxed Science skill.<br /> -High stealth<br /> -Obfuscate and Auspex can be useful.<br /> <br /> This character can't go toe to toe with a Werewolf but, with a bit of time, they can probably take out a pack.<br /> <br /> For a Requiem build you want mental primary and social likely secondary, and Intelligence, Wits, and Composure at at least 3. Put 3-5 points into both Science and Stealth, and nab obfuscate 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:18:17-07:00","id":607207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607193#post607193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same for the werewolf attribute and skills and for the gift i consider: CRIMSON SPASM (add the success on a 15 pool rolls to his strgt so we consider a mean of 8 more dot in strt), BERSERKER\u2019S MIGHT (reduce the damage inflicted by a single source by his Glory Renown (so suppose 5)), Efficient Killer Merit (that private him of defense).<br /> <br /> Now the Vampire have the pool for the attack of (using ride the wave): 20+4 (using 2 vitae)= 24<br /> Werewolf in Gauru attack pool is: 8 str+8 for Crimson+5 brwl = 21<br /> The vampire defense could be. 4+5+5 (celerity)= 14<br /> Werewolf defense (that can't be used if he use Efficient Killer)= 4 wits + 5 athle= 9</div> </div> </div> </div>You've actually given the werewolf too few dice there; Crimson Spasm gives 2 dots of Strength per success, not 1.<br /> <br /> A full-bore Rahu on Crimson Spasm can have average attack dice pools in the 40s.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:35:01-07:00","id":607255,"title":"","content":"Ugh, man. That sounds brutal. I don't mean for this thread to turn into necessarily &quot;top end werewolf vs vampire combat&quot; I am more going for - can this survive? Can this go toe to toe? It could be to kill yes, but it could also be to earn respect from the wolves. I guess I mislead you by the title, its not really a werewolf hunter, someone that lives in between the worlds of the werewolves and the vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","name":"Regentwill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:38:05-07:00","id":607257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607207#post607207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've actually given the werewolf too few dice there; Crimson Spasm gives 2 dots of Strength per success, not 1.<br /> <br /> A full-bore Rahu on Crimson Spasm can have average attack dice pools in the 40s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes sorry my fault. Anyway with that 8 point of bashing (or lethal???) damage more he deal in total 12 damage and the vampire in that example have 15 health dot. A lot of damage but he could survive and using vitae heal for 10 (if bashing) or 5 damage...if he don't kill the werewolf with 29 aggravated damage in this turn or using celerity power in the next turn (without oscuration) the vampire will die <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:40:13-07:00","id":607259,"title":"","content":"To answer that question: Yes, I'd say it could. With the addendum that your storyteller is (hopefully) aware of your intentions and won't deliberately pit you against Werewolves you cannot possibly handle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T17:12:02-07:00","id":607291,"title":"","content":"Anyway there's a devotion (now I don't remember the name tomorrow I'll search for it) that absorb ALL the incoming damage (even aggravated) for a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T18:02:46-07:00","id":607302,"title":"","content":"Juggernaut's Gait. It costs 5 Vitae per turn. Resilience 5, Vigor 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T18:34:18-07:00","id":607331,"title":"","content":"Resilience seems like a good way to go. Vigor and some silvered brass knuckles might help to make the wolves feel more like they are on equal grounds. A dot of Celerity could be good for the interrupt. Smack the werewolf in the gut before they can move then stand there and laugh at their counter attack. Unless they went Gauru, that should earn you some respect. If they do Gauru then you should probably run because I don't think killing werewolves is going to help with the peace. I know getting ashed won't help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T19:50:47-07:00","id":607381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607259#post607259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer that question: Yes, I'd say it could. With the addendum that your storyteller is (hopefully) aware of your intentions and won't deliberately pit you against Werewolves you cannot possibly handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game in question is an online chat setting, I would most likely be dealing with other players of the same XP level as I would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7084-regentwill","name":"Regentwill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T00:25:58-07:00","id":607539,"title":"","content":"So, bringing a weapon isn't an automatic failure in negotiations. It IS pretty common for diplomats to have some security, after all.<br /> <br /> If you avoid stereotypes a little, you can do a lot better with Daeva. Go for 1 dot of each Discipline, or just Majesty 1 and Celerity 2.<br /> <br /> With Majesty 1 you ignore social penalties. It seems little, but what it really does is PRECISELY let you go with silver weapon to face them.<br /> <br /> From there, your actual capacity for negotiating will rely on Attributes and skills. Werewolfs do have Wolf-Blooded and Mortals as pack members nowadays, so you don't have to impress them so much. Some of them can have little respect for weaklings, but believe, most will respect whatever means you got for the Hunt if they are effective.<br /> <br /> And when things get sour, don't think about taking a werewolf down alone. It isn't about vampires not being able to take down one, there are a lot of ways to do so. But first, to be prepared for combat against most werewolfs means to spend most of your resources on combat. Second, a werewolf almost NEVER walks alone.<br /> <br /> Context will play a much larger role on combat, since your reasons to fight, target and goal will be very specifics. If you're a good diplomat, by the way, you can end up hunting a werewolf WITH OTHER werewolfs, and them you will have a function for the pack precisely by not having the same habilities.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you don't manage this, go for fellow kindred to help you. To go alone against a pack in their territory is a suicidal proposition, and to fend off an attack you can surely count on other vampires. Or just run with Celerity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T04:26:23-07:00","id":607632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607193#post607193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO all depends on the &quot;Experience&quot; you give in the built of the two character (vampire and werewolf facing each other). To try to analyze the full power charachter of any race in order to make a totally ipotetical confrontation, and if you want to put the challange just on physical skills I tried to make a simulation about the respective pool:<br /> <br /> For the vampire we consider 5 strgt 5 Brawl 5 BP and 5-4 Athletics, 5 at celerity Vigor and resilence with protean for the Claw and the Unholy Claw.<br /> Same for the werewolf attribute and skills and for the gift i consider: CRIMSON SPASM (add the success on a 15 pool rolls to his strgt so we consider a mean of 8 more dot in strt), BERSERKER\u2019S MIGHT (reduce the damage inflicted by a single source by his Glory Renown (so suppose 5)), Efficient Killer Merit (that private him of defense).<br /> <br /> Now the Vampire have the pool for the attack of (using ride the wave): 20+4 (using 2 vitae)= 24<br /> Werewolf in Gauru attack pool is: 8 str+8 for Crimson+5 brwl = 21<br /> The vampire defense could be. 4+5+5 (celerity)= 14<br /> Werewolf defense (that can't be used if he use Efficient Killer)= 4 wits + 5 athle= 9<br /> <br /> Now consider the werewolf attack first: he use Efficient killer, vampire active celerity and interrupt his attack with his own, so the werewolf can't apply his defense: 24 dice of aggravated damage PLUS 1 vitae to activate vigor and add 5 more dice for a total of 29 dice of aggravated damage......the werewolf can subtract 5 from the success in this dice roll.<br /> <br /> Now consider the case werewolf attack you (maybe cause you won't use the active power of celerity): he make 21+2 for the claw - 14 (vampire defense)= 9 lethal damage.....- 5 using resilence = 4 lethal damage...not so much....Edit: or maybe bashing I'm not sure<br /> <br /> All this to say that both the race have the chance for a fair &quot;duel&quot;.<br /> In the real case where you have to build a normal vampire you could chose different way to defeat a werewolf. Maybe using obfuscate and domination or majesty properly. Anyway all depends on the stats of your opponents.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyway without aggravated damage the story is so far different cause if you don't make more lethal damage of the health of the Gauru in one turn, in the enxt he will completely heal himself for free and you have to start again. In this way at long time you will finish vitae and die :P Or you could use obfuscate to go away or make some kind of backstabb, or dominate to let him go away and save your life <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really sure this is such a fair fight, I mean the vampire in question has 5 celerity, 5 resilience, 5 vigor and 4 protean right? That's 67 experiences worth of disciplines. The Werewolf only has Crimson spasm (15 experiences to get Purity 5) + Berserker's Might (2) + 15 to get Glory 5 = 32 Experiences - less than half what the Vampire has.<br /> <br /> With the other 35 experiences the Wolf could buy; Primal Strength (2) to add + Purity Strength, Slaughterer (2) + Purity Damage, the Relentless Assualt (4) Merit allowing him to retain his defense when making all out attacks, trade 1 attack die for 1 extra damage, the Living Weapon merit (5) to increase his damage by 1 and ignore non-magical armour, the Favoured Form Merit (4) to gain +1 Strength, +1 Stamina in Gauru, Embodiment of the Firstborn (5) to gain +1 Strength, We'll throw in the Fearless Hunter gift (2) to add his Glory Renown (5) against all mind-influencing powers and since we still have 11 experiences unspent we'll pay 5 to get him to Primal Urge 6, pay another 1 to give him the fifth dot of Favoured Form which will let him apply the advanced action quality to brawl rolls in Gauru (roll your pool twice, take the best result) and the last 5 experiences to buy Tongue of Flame from Gift of the Elementals which will let him use fire against the Vampire if he wants.<br /> <br /> The revised dice pools now stand at<br /> <b>Werewolf in Gauru attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 3 (Gauru) + 2 (Merits that increase Strength) + 8 (your number for Crimson Spasm) + 2 for all-out attack + 5 (Gift of Strength) + 5 Brawl -1 (Relentless Assault to gain +1 damage) = 29 dice, with 8-again from Killer Instinct (1st dot Rahu Auspice Gift) and with the advanced action quality<br /> <b>Werewolf in Gauru damage pool:</b> 2 (teeth) + 1 (relentless assualt) + 1 (living weapon) + 5 (slaughterer) = + 9 lethal (Predator's Jaws on p.98 specifies that a Werewolf's bite causes lethal to Vampires even in Hishu)<br /> <b>Werewolf Defense:</b> 9 (Dex/Wits + Athletics)<br /> <b>Werewolf Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 4 (Gauru) + 1 (Favored Form) + 5 (Warrior's Hide - 2nd dot Rahu Auspice Gift) = 20<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 5 (Frenzy) + 5 (Passive Vigor) + 4 (2 vitae) + 5 Brawl = 24<br /> <b>Vampire damage pool:</b> +0 agg (claws of the unholy) + 5 (Active Vigor) = + 5 agg<br /> <b>Vampire defense:</b> 9 (Gauru prevents you from adding any skill to defense so just Dex/Wits + Celerity)<br /> <b>Vampire Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 5 (Resilience) = 15<br /> <br /> I've ignored the Efficient Killer merit because I think the drawback (&quot;This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points&quot;) rules out Vampires (if there's something to contradict this I'd love to know).<br /> <br /> So the Vampire is going to be getting about 5 successes. That's 10 agg damage minus 5 from the Werewolf's Berserker's Might = 5 agg. The Wolf will be getting at least 6 successes (I've no idea how to account for 8-again + advanced action), which is roughly 15 lethal damage minus 5 from Resilience = 10 lethal. With their respective Health pools the Vampire will die after 3 rounds while the Wolf will still be alive (though the Vampire also runs out of Blood after 3 rounds, so he's kind of screwed either way). In my opinion the best option for the Vampire is to forgoe defense and throw everything into a hail mary attack roll (all-out attack + vigor + 4 vitae bonus) and hope he gets lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T04:50:22-07:00","id":607660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607331#post607331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilience seems like a good way to go. Vigor and some silvered brass knuckles might help to make the wolves feel more like they are on equal grounds. A dot of Celerity could be good for the interrupt. Smack the werewolf in the gut before they can move then stand there and laugh at their counter attack. Unless they went Gauru, that should earn you some respect. If they do Gauru then you should probably run because I don't think killing werewolves is going to help with the peace. I know getting ashed won't help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience and Vigor are both good choices for a negotiator to be able to go toe-to-toe in an angry argument that gets a bit physical, but DO NOT use silver weaponry of any kind, including brass knuckles, if you intend to actually do any negotiating whatsoever. Inflict damage with silver and the werewolf will go into Death Rage, at which point you have the choice of trying to stay and kill it, or getting the hell out of Dodge while it levels the surrounding area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T05:17:54-07:00","id":607670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607259#post607259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer that question: Yes, I'd say it could. With the addendum that your storyteller is (hopefully) aware of your intentions and won't deliberately pit you against Werewolves you cannot possibly handle.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is probably the best answer for your actual question - your effectiveness is always going to be down to how your ST makes your enemies.<br /> <br /> Though, I do suggest that, if you're going to be more of a mediator, I'd put some effort into being good at Social Maneuvering. Sympathetic, as a merit, is insanely good for that, as is Fast Talking and Pusher - five doors with the first meeting is nothing to sneer at, and its relatively inexpensive to buy. The first dot of Majesty to make sure you get off to a good impression (it eliminates social penalties, which helps prevent them from looking down, and helps with that initial Impression). You really only need the first dot.<br /> <br /> Talk to your ST about maybe getting some alternative Protean 2 powers, like pheromones, or something, or a social boost. There's no need for all of it to be physical.<br /> <br /> EDIT - <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Regentwill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607381#post607381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game in question is an online chat setting, I would most likely be dealing with other players of the same XP level as I would be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm... in that case... forget what I said above about the ST and enemies. I recommend going with a grapple build - get Protean 4 then invest in Vigor. You get Protean + Vigor (vitae-enhanced) as automatic successes to grapple someone, which is difficult for even Werewolves to overcome. It makes a good lead in to feeding (so invest in Unnatural Affinity too), plus you'll potentially be dealing unhealable agg with damage moves.<br /> <br /> Talk to the STs about how the Choke Hold merit actually works in that game - with the automatic successes from your claws and Vigor, you can easily knock them unconscious, though how long that time will be when Gauru has such a high Stamina is open to question. I don't think the Grapple FS will help in this situation, though it might be something for fighting non-wolves.<br /> <br /> Have a high Wits+Composure score, maybe with some Trained Observer. I suspect that the wolves may end up using Efficient Killer when combined with Cheap Shot, making it a killing blow if their Dex+Subterfuge check beats your perception check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-30-2015, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T05:36:36-07:00","id":607732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607632#post607632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've ignored the Efficient Killer merit because I think the drawback (&quot;This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points&quot;) rules out Vampires (if there's something to contradict this I'd love to know).</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, vampires are known for not getting back up if you rip out their heart or tear off their head, so I imagine that those would count, especially if our wolf is in Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T07:08:15-07:00","id":607852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607732#post607732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, vampires are known for not getting back up if you rip out their heart or tear off their head, so I imagine that those would count, especially if our wolf is in Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more given pause by the &quot;living&quot; part of the requirement. I mean, it seems obvious that the intent is &quot;this doesn't work on spirits&quot; but what happens with crossovers (Geists, Mummies, and Prometheans are all questionably &quot;living&quot;). Clearly the only right answer is it's up to the Storyteller, but I was wondering if perhaps the Devs had said anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T08:00:38-07:00","id":607897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607660#post607660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resilience and Vigor are both good choices for a negotiator to be able to go toe-to-toe in an angry argument that gets a bit physical, but DO NOT use silver weaponry of any kind, including brass knuckles, if you intend to actually do any negotiating whatsoever. Inflict damage with silver and the werewolf will go into Death Rage, at which point you have the choice of trying to stay and kill it, or getting the hell out of Dodge while it levels the surrounding area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not that familiar with Werewolf. If damage from silver always, or even usually, causes Death Rage then it would be best to leave that stuff at home for the same reason the vampire shouldn't fight Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T08:32:22-07:00","id":607926,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't use silver&quot; and &quot;Don't fight Gauru&quot; are both good tips, but you can't always avoid breaking the second and if you <i>do</i> break the second breaking the first as well is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T08:52:54-07:00","id":607942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=607852#post607852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more given pause by the &quot;living&quot; part of the requirement. I mean, it seems obvious that the intent is &quot;this doesn't work on spirits&quot; but what happens with crossovers (Geists, Mummies, and Prometheans are all questionably &quot;living&quot;). Clearly the only right answer is it's up to the Storyteller, but I was wondering if perhaps the Devs had said anything</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm... that's a good point. By that rationale, ghosts wouldn't be hit with efficient killer either. While vampire's aren't <i>dead</i>, they're not quite alive either.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd totally be all down with using efficient killer on humans, hosts, claimed, and fellow wolves, as well as those spirits that resemble living creatures (elemental or artifice spirits, not so much). But if we're excluding the undead like ghosts, then yeah.<br /> <br /> I feel compelled to point out that Prometheans are fully 100% alive from a metaphysical standpoint, though they probably fail the discernible weak point test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-30-2015, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:32:02-07:00","id":608509,"title":"","content":"Just a question. What about grappling move to fight a werewolf and winning (using vitae and always in frenzy) the contested roll str+brawl+ other stuff feeding him to death?? Could it be possible??? And how many turns does it requires?? In that case spending vitae wouldn't be a problem becouse vampire fill his stocks every turn. What do you think? Am I losing something? I think in that case the dice pool could be more fair...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:29:15-07:00","id":608748,"title":"","content":"Using willpower, a vampire can feed using the Assault or Kiss so I would think it is definitely possible. How long depends on how much essence a werewolf burns until they break free or die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:39:13-07:00","id":608754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=608748#post608748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using willpower, a vampire can feed using the Assault or Kiss so I would think it is definitely possible. How long depends on how much essence a werewolf burns until they break free or die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why depends on essence he burn??? The vampire would try to finish the blood of the werewolf not kill him damaging him.<br /> Anyway the number of vitae obtained per turn is equal to the number of successes rolled in the contrasted roll? Or just the successes &quot;in excess&quot; of that roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:47:01-07:00","id":608762,"title":"","content":"Because werewolves can spend 1 Essence to turn their per-turn bashing regeneration to lethal regeneration.<br /> <br /> You'll need the Unnatural Affinity merit, too. And obviously to find werewolves alone somehow, which might be hard once werewolves start going to meet him and don't come back. Or a variety of gifts or merits that would allow him to escape. Or a simple good roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T04:06:23-07:00","id":609247,"title":"","content":"Grappling is about equal for wolves and vamps. Wolves get Primal Strength as a bonus to strength, plus form bonuses, 8-again if Rahu, and a bit from Favored form. Vamps get double Vigor (costs 1 vitae), frenzy (need BP), blood buff, and can use a chain / blood scourge / protean claws, making it more likely the vamps control the grapple.<br /> <br /> In short - wolves can get +purity+4 dice bonus, but also 8-again and maybe Advanced action (roll twice, take better) at PU4, while vamps get +BP+vigor+blood buff+weapon bonus. Wolves also get more damage if they succeed at the grapple check, but vamps can get much higher dice pools. Unfortunately for the vamp, a Choke Hold or agg claws are the only option for making the wolf stop, otherwise the vamp runs out of blood and the wolf wins (assuming Gauru lasts long enough, or Death Rage), since a Damage move isn't damaging enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-31-2015, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:17:54-07:00","id":609272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=609247#post609247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grappling is about equal for wolves and vamps. Wolves get Primal Strength as a bonus to strength, plus form bonuses, 8-again if Rahu, and a bit from Favored form. Vamps get double Vigor (costs 1 vitae), frenzy (need BP), blood buff, and can use a chain / blood scourge / protean claws, making it more likely the vamps control the grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why get double Vigor?? the vigor's active effect doesn't apply only to the weapon?? Considering a grappling action it could be applied anyway?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=609247#post609247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short - wolves can get +purity+4 dice bonus, but also 8-again and maybe Advanced action (roll twice, take better) at PU4, while vamps get +BP+vigor+blood buff+weapon bonus. Wolves also get more damage if they succeed at the grapple check, but vamps can get much higher dice pools. Unfortunately for the vamp, a Choke Hold or agg claws are the only option for making the wolf stop, otherwise the vamp runs out of blood and the wolf wins (assuming Gauru lasts long enough, or Death Rage), since a Damage move isn't damaging enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I according with you if the goal of the grappling movment is to make damage. But what about if the vampire just drain out all the blood (vitae) from the Gauru?? How many vitae per turn could he steal? Drain out werewolf blood prevent the vampire to go out of vitae right?<br /> <br /> Another thing: The vampire could have 4 points in Coils of the Wyrm that passively adds BP to Health point, and Defence (that could replace the missing of the skill value in the defense value), and with the merit: Riding the wave could add + 3 to any attacks and + 2 to defense using willpower. It could be a further help to raise the dices pools. Is it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-31-2015, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:44:19-07:00","id":609287,"title":"","content":"The game doesn't work blood in the werewolf system separately from her health track, so no shortcuts here: you surely have a good strategy, but you're going to deal with her regeneration all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:32:16-07:00","id":609314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=609272#post609272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why get double Vigor?? the vigor's active effect doesn't apply only to the weapon?? Considering a grappling action it could be applied anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div> The vigor's active effect applies as a weapon bonus. And certain appropriate weapons can be used in grapples as an equipment bous. So, you can be adding Vigor not just to your strength, but your equipment bonus as well. Thus, adding Vigor twice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I according with you if the goal of the grappling movment is to make damage. But what about if the vampire just drain out all the blood (vitae) from the Gauru?? How many vitae per turn could he steal? Drain out werewolf blood prevent the vampire to go out of vitae right? </div> </div> </div> Vitae is represented by lethal damage. Going strictly by mechanics, a werewolf in Wasu-Im would never run out of vitae, since all damage is healed at start of turn, and that includes the damage from drinking the vitae. The ST would have to make a call on that issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing: The vampire could have 4 points in Coils of the Wyrm that passively adds BP to Health point, and Defence (that could replace the missing of the skill value in the defense value), and with the merit: Riding the wave could add + 3 to any attacks and + 2 to defense using willpower. It could be a further help to raise the dices pools. Is it right? </div> </div> </div> The Coil can add to Defense (but then, so does Celerity) to avoid being grappled in the first place, but once in a grapple, Defense doesn't matter. And I didn't really count the willpower, since both sides can use it to augment their dice pools.<br /> <br /> Even with Celerity, you'll never get your defense high enough to completely avoid being hit by a combat-based werewolf of equal EXP without Dodging. If you're going that route, best to just use Celerity to keep your distance and use silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-31-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:24:32-07:00","id":610027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=608509#post608509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question. What about grappling move to fight a werewolf and winning (using vitae and always in frenzy) the contested roll str+brawl+ other stuff feeding him to death?? Could it be possible??? And how many turns does it requires?? In that case spending vitae wouldn't be a problem becouse vampire fill his stocks every turn. What do you think? Am I losing something? I think in that case the dice pool could be more fair...</div> </div> </div> </div>Get caps from your fangs made with real silver and a few levels of Blood Potency and that might be a viable tactic. (You will do your blood potency level in damage.) But I expect after a few incidents of that, werewolves may decide to open up combat with a well placed fist to your character's mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:37:37-07:00","id":610037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=609247#post609247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grappling is about equal for wolves and vamps. Wolves get Primal Strength as a bonus to strength, plus form bonuses, 8-again if Rahu, and a bit from Favored form. Vamps get double Vigor (costs 1 vitae), frenzy (need BP), blood buff, and can use a chain / blood scourge / protean claws, making it more likely the vamps control the grapple.<br /> <br /> In short - wolves can get +purity+4 dice bonus, but also 8-again and maybe Advanced action (roll twice, take better) at PU4, while vamps get +BP+vigor+blood buff+weapon bonus. Wolves also get more damage if they succeed at the grapple check, but vamps can get much higher dice pools. Unfortunately for the vamp, a Choke Hold or agg claws are the only option for making the wolf stop, otherwise the vamp runs out of blood and the wolf wins (assuming Gauru lasts long enough, or Death Rage), since a Damage move isn't damaging enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Uratha can also benefit from Unchained, gaining up to Cunning in additional grapple dice iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:09:04-07:00","id":610064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610027#post610027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get caps from your fangs made with real silver and a few levels of Blood Potency and that might be a viable tactic. (You will do your blood potency level in damage.) But I expect after a few incidents of that, werewolves may decide to open up combat with a well placed fist to your character's mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And in that case the character could interrupt this action with celerity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But what power allow to deal aggravated damage with silver fangs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:43:03-07:00","id":610110,"title":"","content":"Vampires can do a feed move if they successfully grapple someone. They can take 1 vitae per success (up to their blood potency) dealing 1 lethal per vitae taken.<br /> A vampire's fangs count as zero lethal weapons in a brawl check. So if they're capped with real silver it would be aggravated versus a werewolf. (And may be subject to the Scarred condition at ST's discretion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:57:09-07:00","id":610204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610064#post610064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in that case the character could interrupt this action with celerity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can interrupt in Urshul form, or use the Hit and Run merit. It would be up to a Clash of Wills, with an interrupt versus an interrupt, but the ability is there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:19:20-07:00","id":610308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll need the Unnatural Affinity merit, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It is only to consider Uratha blood as vampire blood. But not to consider it as blood per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:51:59-07:00","id":610596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610308#post610308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. It is only to consider Uratha blood as vampire blood. But not to consider it as blood per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually open to debate. The merit is the only time supernatural blood is mentioned, so its possible for an ST to say that wolf blood is undigestable without it. Not like there aren't tropes of werewolf blood being bad for vamps in some stories, and being really good in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:59:22-07:00","id":610617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610037#post610037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha can also benefit from Unchained, gaining up to Cunning in additional grapple dice iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div> huh. So it does, and it doesn't specify you must break away. I missed that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610204#post610204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can interrupt in Urshul form, or use the Hit and Run merit. It would be up to a Clash of Wills, with an interrupt versus an interrupt, but the ability is there.</div> </div> </div> </div> but then, we wouldn't be in Gauru, which means less healing, and less damage. defense would play into the Battle much more. Completely different situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:30:45-07:00","id":611048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=610617#post610617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but then, we wouldn't be in Gauru, which means less healing, and less damage. defense would play into the Battle much more. Completely different situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can change reflexively by spending a point of Essence or being at the right harmony, and Gauru will heal damage done in turns before you changed just as well as it does in turns after.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:20:55-07:00","id":611169,"title":"","content":"I'm well aware. However, the damage is healed at the START of your turn, meaning that we're talking about at least two rounds worth of damage that's not healed immediately, which can be potentially deadly - its rare to have someone in one turn that can one-shot you, but over two turns? Completely viable. You could also regenerate through essence, but this means that's less essence being used for Gifts or other effects per turn (the shifting cost can also reduce essence per turn use). Which is not favorable.<br /> <br /> Now, if you're focusing on the Rapid Shifting FS (or whatever its called) instead of the three preferred form merits, that's a valid tactic. That comes with its own complications, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:45:19-07:00","id":611219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=611169#post611169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is not favorable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree to an extent. Once you're talking about opponents with silver weapons or fangs or anything that can do a lot of damage, that first attack which can be used to cause Arm Wrack, to Disarm, or to make a called shot to the face, can make all the difference. If you have the capacity to off or disable a target in one shot, getting the first turn saves a lot of danger. It's a conditional thing, but everything in this thread is, and that doesn't mean it's always 'not favorable.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:20:19-07:00","id":611271,"title":"","content":"The Hit and Run facet can be used in any form, though, so it makes that aspect of Celerity a moot point. In fact, Hit and Run has the advantage of not being limited by uses per scene, so strictly speaking the werewolf wins if you're trying to out-interrupt each other. If we're talking about a straight up brawl, then all these abilities do is cancel each other out and we are left with the basic advantages of the splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:28:59-07:00","id":611564,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't we focus on the Vampire guy? There are a lot of possible builds for the werewolfs he can potentialy enter in conflict with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:37:04-07:00","id":611577,"title":"","content":"Outside of gaining every attribute and skill and discipline and sorcery there's no one build that can handle every werewolf they'll have to deal with. The original poster had a 'build' in the first post that would work pretty well for dealing with certain werewolves in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:10:53-07:00","id":611637,"title":"","content":"That said, as has been brought up in another thread at some point by PenDragon, a vampire with Primeval Miasma and a predisposition for grappling can fair pretty well against pretty much anything that doesn't have immediate access to fire or sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:52:54-07:00","id":611703,"title":"","content":"Or Breath of Air, which they might use to trap the cloud of smoke into a jar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:15:25-07:00","id":611748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=611703#post611703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Breath of Air, which they might use to trap the cloud of smoke into a jar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but it would probably cause a Clash of Wills since Primeval Miasma allows the vampire to control how big of an area its fog form can spread and Breath of Air would be attempting to condense it into a small enough area as to fit into a jar. And since the power lasts indefinitely unless canceled or damaged by sunlight the vampire would receive a fairly sizable bonus to the roll off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:28:11-07:00","id":614768,"title":"","content":"If I were an undead ruler and I needed someone to keep Werewolves in check in my territory I would NOT rely on a Gangrel brute, that is a dangerous one shot crap weapon. I would rely on a tough and intelligent agent capable of actually filling the role (could be any clan really). Vampires who tend to use brawn are not going to live long enough and are just going to make matters worse.<br /> <br /> As in all other facet of life and violent situations in particular it is all about stacking the card as much in your favor. This means that knowledge about the situation and opponent are by far more important than your dots in Vigor or Protean. Knowing what is enough manpower and/or controlling the environment or when to strike is whats going to make you a successful enforcer. A stupid enforcer go in and fight without knowing they will win no matter what.<br /> <br /> You can discuss what power will do what in a physical confrontation, but if you enter into such a situation without being prepared and armed to the teeth you are just being stupid. Relying on personal prowess are just throwing the dice and hoping for the best. This will eventually get you killed once you encounter an unexpected factor.<br /> <br /> Creating a character with the intent of physically beating a Werewolf in single combat are in my opinion the least effective way dealing with the problem. I have no problem with a vampire being a physically powerful character so they can survive an encounter with a Werewolf. But if you are physically threatened your first priority should be retreat and not offense, you never know what other surprises awaits you of you engage with no means to escape. You will in this instance need to retreat and come back tenfold in strength. You NEVER fight with equal odds, that is just stupid and a borderline naive way to solve a problem.<br /> <br /> Players in my campaigns are very reluctant to engage in physical confrontations since they are so uncertain (unless the outcome are clear)... anything from the dice rolls going against them to not being able to controlling the situation most of the time. This is true no matter what role-playing system we play... I usually do not reward wanton violence just to spice up the game... to me violence need to make sense and be dramatic and realistic to some degree. A player character that tend over-commit will often also die... often sooner rather than later... this is very realistic.<br /> <br /> Enough ranting on my part... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:36:55-07:00","id":614769,"title":"","content":"The thing is though, with werewolves you <i>need</i> a fair bit of muscle to enact the &quot;and then we punch them&quot; part of the plan. You can be the most brilliant ambusher in the world, but it's going to diddly squat when the werewolf you expertly lured into the death trap proceeds to just get back up and rip your head off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T03:50:23-07:00","id":614777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/607106-concept-werewolf-hunter?p=614769#post614769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is though, with werewolves you <i>need</i> a fair bit of muscle to enact the &quot;and then we punch them&quot; part of the plan. You can be the most brilliant ambusher in the world, but it's going to diddly squat when the werewolf you expertly lured into the death trap proceeds to just get back up and rip your head off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is the part of &quot;know your enemy&quot; and being prepared... that is part of the job description and if you don't know the capabilities of your opponent you have already failed.<br /> <br /> It is not about being good at ambush tactics, it is about so many more things that contribute to success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:31:51-07:00","id":615704,"title":"","content":"Given that the main goal is to make a diplomat, I would stick to Daeva. 1 dot of Majesty just to lubricate things a little, 2 dots of Celerity to deal with whatever have to be dealt with. Including simple run, but also good for combat.<br /> <br /> From this, use your mind. Proximity with the Uratha can be worked by the rest of the sheet, and they are people, not mindless brutes, even if with the ability to become mindless brutes for some time. Guess what, vampires also have this ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}